  annotation "note_1771574929436_1", anchor: "a Nightshelf raiding party shattered the Codex against the volcanic vents near the Lower Meridian", text: "The Lower Meridian vents are Nightshelf-adjacent territory. The Codex was an Aurora factional artifact whose imprimatur, as stated three sentences earlier, functioned as a transit credential through Holdborn trade routes. If Holdborn was extending Codex-backed passage authority into corridors the Nightshelf considered theirs — and deep-ice trade records from that period suggest exactly this — then 'raiding party' is doing considerable narrative work. No witnesses survived, which means the framing was chosen by the faction that lost the artifact, not the one that broke it. I wrote 'raiding party' because the sources are unanimous and I am bound by them. The margins are not so bound.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574929436_2", anchor: "I note without comment that the Flipper Accord has been renegotiated more times than the public record reflects", text: "Three times. In secret. The drafts are in administrative ice so deep I needed two full shifts to reach them, and they had been filed under provisions logistics — deliberately mislabeled, or labeled by someone who understood that provisions is what the Accord actually governs. Xuezhaihei's vision of the Codex's pages as seals corresponding to renegotiations is recorded as prophecy. I am not prepared to call it that. But the number of sealed pages in the surviving fragment descriptions is three, and I have not been able to set that aside.", type: :correction, display: :full
